Update getMessages() in prompt.ts to reconstruct message history from loaded turn impulses.

## Logic

After renegotiation, only messages whose turn impulse is loaded should be included in context.

## Implementation

In src/session/prompt.ts, in the getMessages() function:

```typescript
// After renegotiation completes, filter messages by loaded impulses
const { SessionMemory } = await import("./session-memory")
const impulses = await SessionMemory.listImpulses(input.sessionID)
const turnImpulses = impulses.filter(i => i.type === "messageHistory")

// Get message IDs from loaded turn impulses
const loadedMessageIDs = new Set<string>()
for (const impulse of turnImpulses) {
  if (impulse.loaded && impulse.pointer.type === "messageHistory") {
    for (const msgID of impulse.pointer.messageIDs) {
      loadedMessageIDs.add(msgID)
    }
  }
}

// Filter messages to only include those in loaded turns
messages = messages.filter(msg => loadedMessageIDs.has(msg.info.id))

log.info("filtered messages by loaded impulses", {
  sessionID: input.sessionID,
  totalBeforeFilter: (await MessageV2.stream(input.sessionID)).length,
  afterFilter: messages.length,
  loadedTurns: turnImpulses.filter(i => i.loaded).length,
})
```

## Placement

Add this filtering AFTER the renegotiation call succeeds (around line ~750 after the renegotiate() call).

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Loads turn impulses after renegotiation
- [ ] Filters messages by loaded impulse state
- [ ] Only includes messages from loaded turns
- [ ] Logs filtering statistics
- [ ] No compilation errors
- [ ] No infinite loops (check carefully)

